### Mini Gemini Code Guide: **Java OOP Principles & Concurrency**

Java is a robust, class-based, object-oriented language compiled to bytecode running on the JVM.

#### 1. Java Thread Safety & Encapsulation
Here is a thread-safe singleton manager class demonstrating OOP concepts:

```java
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

public class CareerMentor {
    private static volatile CareerMentor instance;
    private final String name;
    private final AtomicInteger sessionsCount;

    // Private Constructor prevents external initialization
    private CareerMentor(String name) {
        this.name = name;
        this.sessionsCount = new AtomicInteger(0);
    }

    // Thread-safe Double-Checked Locking Singleton Pattern
    public static CareerMentor getInstance(String name) {
        if (instance == null) {
            synchronized (CareerMentor.class) {
                if (instance == null) {
                    instance = new CareerMentor(name);
                } 
            }
        }
        return instance;
    }

    public int incrementSessions() {
        return sessionsCount.incrementAndGet();
    }

    public String getMentorGreeting(String role) {
        return "Welcome to Java Coaching, aspiring " + role + "! Sessions run: " + sessionsCount.get();
    }
}
```

#### 2. Key Java OOP Standards:
*   **Solid Principles:** Design with Single Responsibility, Open/Closed inheritance, and Dependency Inversion.
*   **Concurrency:** Use `java.util.concurrent` tools (ExecutorService, Atomic variables) instead of raw thread handles.

