### Mini Gemini Algorithms Guide: **Big O Complexity & Searching/Sorting**

Algorithms define logic execution, graded by Big O notation for time and space scalability as inputs grow.

#### 1. Binary Search Implementation (Iterative & O(log N) Time)
Here is a type-safe binary search algorithm in TypeScript. It requires a pre-sorted array:

```typescript
function binarySearch(arr: number[], target: number): number {
    let left = 0;
    let right = arr.length - 1;

    while (left <= right) {
        // Safe mid-point calculation avoiding integer overflows
        const mid = Math.floor(left + (right - left) / 2);

        if (arr[mid] === target) {
            return mid; // Index found
        }

        if (arr[mid] < target) {
            left = mid + 1; // Search right half
        } else {
            right = mid - 1; // Search left half
        }
    }

    return -1; // Target not present
}

// Example Execution
const sortedData = [10, 22, 34, 47, 55, 68, 72, 89];
console.log("Found target at index:", binarySearch(sortedData, 55)); // Output: 4
```

#### 2. Big O Summary Table:
| Algorithm | Best Time | Average Time | Worst Time | Space Complexity |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Binary Search** | $O(1)$ | $O(\log N)$ | $O(\log N)$ | $O(1)$ (Iterative) |
| **Quicksort** | $O(N \log N)$ | $O(N \log N)$ | $O(N^2)$ | $O(\log N)$ (Stack recursion) |
| **Mergesort** | $O(N \log N)$ | $O(N \log N)$ | $O(N \log N)$ | $O(N)$ (Auxiliary storage) |

#### 3. Mentor DSA Tip:
In interviews for **{dreamRole}** positions, code solutions iteratively first if recursive stack limits present concerns. Always declare time and space constraints before typing code.

